#!/bin/sh
# Prepares a Linux host (Ubuntu or Debian, as root) to run a Rudder Cloud home:
# Docker, rsync, the sysctls agents need, the data disk at /srv/workspace and
# the systemd units. Safe to run again. It does not start the home: `rudder
# cloud host` writes /etc/rudder/home.env and /etc/rudder/image, then starts
# rudder-home.service.
#
#   sudo ./rudder-host-setup [--data-disk /dev/nvme1n1]
#
# The data disk is formatted only when it holds no filesystem and no partitions.
set -eu

HERE=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)
DATA=/srv/workspace
LABEL=rudder-ws
DISK=""
while [ "$#" -gt 0 ]; do
  case "$1" in
    --data-disk) DISK=${2:?--data-disk needs a device}; shift 2 ;;
    --data-disk=*) DISK=${1#*=}; shift ;;
    -h|--help) sed -n '2,10p' "$0"; exit 0 ;;
    *) echo "rudder-host-setup: unknown argument $1" >&2; exit 64 ;;
  esac
done

[ "$(id -u)" = 0 ] || { echo "rudder-host-setup: run it as root (sudo)" >&2; exit 1; }

if ! command -v docker >/dev/null 2>&1 || ! command -v rsync >/dev/null 2>&1; then
  export DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive
  apt-get update -q
  apt-get install -y -q docker.io rsync
fi
systemctl enable --now docker >/dev/null

install -m 644 "$HERE/90-rudder.conf" /etc/sysctl.d/90-rudder.conf
systemctl restart systemd-sysctl.service 2>/dev/null || sysctl -e -q -p /etc/sysctl.d/90-rudder.conf || true

mkdir -p "$DATA"
if [ -n "$DISK" ]; then
  [ -b "$DISK" ] || { echo "rudder-host-setup: $DISK is not a block device" >&2; exit 1; }
  if [ "$(blkid -s LABEL -o value "$DISK" 2>/dev/null || true)" = "$LABEL" ]; then
    : # set up by an earlier run
  elif blkid -p "$DISK" >/dev/null 2>&1 || [ "$(lsblk -n -o NAME "$DISK" | wc -l)" -ne 1 ]; then
    echo "rudder-host-setup: $DISK already holds a filesystem or partitions; not touching it" >&2
    exit 1
  else
    echo "rudder-host-setup: formatting $DISK as ext4 ($LABEL)"
    mkfs.ext4 -q -L "$LABEL" -m 0 "$DISK"
  fi
  grep -q "^LABEL=$LABEL " /etc/fstab || echo "LABEL=$LABEL $DATA ext4 defaults,noatime,nofail 0 2" >> /etc/fstab
  systemctl daemon-reload
  mountpoint -q "$DATA" || mount "$DATA"
fi
# The worker runs as uid 1500 (cloud/worker/root-bootstrap.sh).
chown 1500:1500 "$DATA"

mkdir -p /etc/rudder
chmod 700 /etc/rudder
install -m 755 "$HERE/rudder-home-start" /usr/local/bin/rudder-home-start
install -m 755 "$HERE/rudder-home-apply-update" /usr/local/bin/rudder-home-apply-update
install -m 644 "$HERE/rudder-home.service" "$HERE/rudder-home-update.service" "$HERE/rudder-home-update.path" /etc/systemd/system/
systemctl daemon-reload
systemctl enable rudder-home.service rudder-home-update.path >/dev/null 2>&1
systemctl start rudder-home-update.path
echo "rudder-host-setup: ready ($DATA: $(df -h --output=size "$DATA" | tail -n 1 | tr -d ' '))"
